  "published": "2026-11-23T08:05:32.61Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- `TzDataRule.GetTransitionDate` throws `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` for a weekday on or after February 29, such as `Sun>=29`, in a common year, which zic rejects, instead of returning a date in March.\n- `new SystemTimeWithGregorianCalendar(ISystemTime)` throws `ArgumentException` for a default `SystemTimeWithGregorianCalendar`, which wraps no system time.\n\nFixed:\n- `TzDataTimezone.CompareTo(object)` returns a positive number for `null`, as `IComparable.CompareTo` requires, instead of throwing `ArgumentNullException`.\n- `TzDataRule.GetTransitionDate` counts a weekday on or before February 29, such as `Sun<=29`, back from February 28 in a common year, as zic does, instead of returning March 1.\n- `ToDateTime` and `ToDateOnly` throw a documented `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` for any system time outside the range of `DateTime` or `DateOnly`, instead of an undocumented `OverflowException` far from the epoch.\n- `ToTimeOnly`, and the `Hour`, `Minute` and `Second` of a `SystemTimeWithGregorianCalendar`, give the time of day of a `UnixTime` however far it is from the epoch, instead of throwing `OverflowException`.\n- `AsUnixTime` and `AsDosDateTime` no longer return null for a `SystemTimeWithGregorianCalendar` that wraps another one, and it now equals a single wrapper of the same value.\n- The package now includes its XML documentation, so IntelliSense shows member descriptions.",
